// False-9 System manager archetype — hand-authored, NOT LLM-baked.
//
// Modern positional tactician using a false 9 to pull opposing CBs out of
// shape. CF drops into midfield; wide forwards make underlapping runs
// into the vacated central channel. Moderate risk appetite (0.55) — the
// false 9 needs space + time to manufacture the CB-disorganization +
// commits midfield numbers forward to support. HIGH possession preference
// (0.80) — possession control is the mechanism that makes the false-9
// pull effective; without it the system collapses to a striker-less attack.
//
// Q32 raw-bits computation (BAKE-TIME math; never in canonical paths):
//   risk_appetite:         0.55 × 2^32 = 2_362_232_012.8 → 2_362_232_013
//   possession_preference: 0.80 × 2^32 = 3_435_973_836.8 → 3_435_973_837
//
// Tactical archetype reference resolves to content/sources/archetypes/
//   false-9-system.ron  (validated at load time by ContentStore).
//
// Authored 2026-05-17 (T2-1c).

ManagerArchetype(
    schema_version: 1,
    id: "fwh.core:manager.false-9-system",
    display_name: "False-9 System",
    tactical_archetype_id: "fwh.core:archetype.false-9-system",
